{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "CAE-AMI-V1.0-I01", "AIMName": "1CAE-AMI-V1.0-I01"},
  "Header":               "CAE-AMI-V1.0",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Management Interface: the one AIM of Audio Scene Management that touches the boundary of the Composite. Its right-hand side serves the Editing AIMs - Audio Object Editing, Audio Scene Editing, Speech Object Editing, Speech Scene Editing and Multimodal Scene Editing - exactly as the boundary of the Module served them before: it gives each its User Command, its User PoV and the Objects and Scenes that arrive, and it gives the boundary what they output, with the User Command responses. Its left-hand side is the boundary: User Commands, User PoVs, Audio Objects, Audio Scenes, Speech Objects and Speech Scenes in; the edited Objects, the Scenes, the Multimodal Scene and the User Command responses out. It also takes the commands of an application interface: an Application JSON Instance (MMC-AJI) whose ApplicationSchemaURI is the schema of the User Command that its Access names (CommandSchema) and whose Instance conforms to it is turned into a User Command request and sent to the Editing AIMs as any other; the response of the Editing AIMs is returned in an Application JSON Instance that names the instance it answers. A command that does not conform is answered by a response that reports it failed. A list of everything (Kind All) is sent to every Editing AIM and the answers are merged into one response. It does no editing.",

